>Can wizards really survive ?

Wizards start the game with equipment to keep them alive for quite some time.

They always start with an athame and a cloak of magic resistance, providing
long lasting engravings and multi-trap protection respectively.  In addition,
they start with two rings; invisibility, regeneration, conflict, levitation,
and teleport control rings CAN all prolong your lifespan to the endgame.

They also start with a wand, potions, and scrolls which may or may not be
useful in prolonging your life.  If they start with blindfold and or magic
marker, they have even higher chances of being successful.

When I play wizards, I have three goals for the first few levels:
1) lower my AC
2) gain poison resistance
3) find a longsword and make Excalibur

4) gain telapathy   (of course...  this should be a goal for every class)

I try to avoid things like sacrificing at altars, robbing shops, kicking sinks,
polypiling, etc.  until I have accomplished all of the above.  There are always
exceptions in nethack, but that's my general plan.  I try to shoot for at least
a 0 AC for levels 1-6, -4 for levels 6-12, and -10 or better below level 12.

Disclaimer: I do not polypile or kick sinks.

If I happen to get an early wish, I always wish for speed boots.  Wizards don't
get much benefit from gray dragon scale mail since they already have a cloak of
magic resistance.
